      'bilirubin is the yellow orange pigment produced when old red blood cells are broken down the haem is converted to biliverdin then to bilirubin unconjugated bilirubin is fat soluble carried on albumin to the liver where it is conjugated made water soluble and excreted in bile into the gut where bacteria turn it into stercobilin which colours the faeces brown a small amount goes to the kidneys and colours urine yellow',
