      'the endocrine pancreas is only about 1 to 2 percent of the tissue about a million scattered islets of langerhans that secrete hormones straight into the blood insulin from beta cells lowers blood glucose glucagon from alpha cells raises it somatostatin from delta cells inhibits both diseases exocrine failure causes malabsorption endocrine failure causes diabetes',
